CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^\[main\.assigns\.\d+\] line \d+ Check that t is assignable: FAILURE$
--
--
Checks that a variable declared before a loop whose address is taken is not a
loop local, even if it is dead at the loop head: pointers may reach it, so it
must be in the loop assigns clause.
